1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,740
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:06,559
In this lesson, we will automate a
repeatable task with visible outcomes.

3
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:11,289
Manual copying between systems costs
time and hides failures when there

4
00:00:11,289 --> 00:00:13,350
is no recorded execution history.

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:16,819
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,819 --> 00:00:18,719
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,909 --> 00:00:23,329
A workflow posts new calls to a team
channel, and a custom field records

8
00:00:23,329 --> 00:00:25,110
the fire district on each call.

9
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:28,789
Automate repeated administrative
steps and connect Rez grid

10
00:00:28,789 --> 00:00:30,380
to the other systems you use.

11
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:34,249
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:34,249 --> 00:00:36,480
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:37,409
Workflows.

14
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:40,179
Automations triggered
by department events.

15
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:44,629
Start with one workflow for a task
you repeat, and review its runs.

16
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:46,430
User-defined fields.

17
00:00:46,849 --> 00:00:50,249
Custom fields on calls,
personnel and other records.

18
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:53,020
Add only the fields you must capture.

19
00:00:53,239 --> 00:00:55,610
API and MCP integrations.

20
00:00:56,309 --> 00:00:59,600
API and MCP access for other systems.

21
00:01:00,009 --> 00:01:04,019
Create credentials for each integration
and limit what they can access.

22
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,030
New Workflow.

23
00:01:05,490 --> 00:01:07,239
Create an automation workflow.

24
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:10,620
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready, and

25
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,750
decide who owns each automation.

26
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,099
Workflow Runs.

27
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:17,550
The history of workflow
runs, including failures.

28
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:20,860
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready, and

29
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:22,949
decide who owns each automation.

30
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:24,940
Import and migration planning.

31
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:28,509
Plan moving your data from
another system into Rez grid.

32
00:01:28,929 --> 00:01:31,979
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready, and

33
00:01:31,979 --> 00:01:34,140
decide who owns each automation.

34
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:37,269
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

35
00:01:37,789 --> 00:01:38,349
Step 1.

36
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:42,340
Choose one event and an approved
destination for a workflow.

37
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:43,450
Step 2.

38
00:01:43,969 --> 00:01:48,139
Configure the workflow action, data
mapping, and integration access.

39
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,309
Step 3.

40
00:01:49,729 --> 00:01:54,379
Trigger a controlled demo event and review
Workflow Runs for success or failure.

41
00:01:54,589 --> 00:01:56,099
Now verify the result.

42
00:01:56,459 --> 00:02:00,770
Confirm the intended action at the
destination and inspect the recorded run.

43
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:04,639
Test a controlled failure and
document who owns retries.

44
00:02:05,099 --> 00:02:09,259
A common problem to watch for:
A saved workflow is not evidence

45
00:02:09,259 --> 00:02:11,199
that its destination received data.

46
00:02:11,529 --> 00:02:15,109
Protected content requires the
separately reviewed egress path.

47
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:16,820
Your practice task is simple.

48
00:02:17,279 --> 00:02:20,980
Create a demo-only new-call
workflow and inspect its run.

49
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:26,330
Record successful and failed execution
evidence, owner, and recovery steps.

50
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:30,649
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

51
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:34,529
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
